      "selectionScope": "Selected bodies and matching craft references were read. The entire motion profile was not loaded. No SVG workflow was selected because the object is ordinary HTML/CSS geometry, with no SVG artwork or asset.",
      "application": {
        "navigation": "Data resolves outside capture. One guarded synchronous callback owns DOM/title/history/focus/scroll. Rejected ready/finished promises never replay the application update. Unique temporary identities follow the selected study and are removed by current-transition ownership.",
        "captureBoundary": "A flat outer presentation wrapper surrounds the closed object's self-contained camera/subtree. Preserved travel/tilt/hinge nodes never receive a capture name. Initial flat-leaf capture visibly separated the cover from its backing during navigation, so the complete-object wrapper was retained after rendered review.",
        "choreography": "Five tracks share document.timeline.currentTime: travel, tilt, left-edge hinge, paper shift and annotation. Each owns a separate node. Open/closed base styles own the settled pose; filled effects are cancelled after settling. Retarget samples current presentation, generations invalidate obsolete completion work, and expected cancellation rejections are handled.",
        "lifecycle": "Each mounted sequence owns its listeners and animation handles. Navigation disposes that sequence. Replay replaces prior effects; pause waits for native readiness in verification. Live reduced motion skips native capture and settles active tracks without hiding content.",
        "composition": "One warm paper direction with editorial serif headings, quiet metadata and original geometric covers. The same two paper objects carry content through collection and detail views; no separate showcase gallery, theme picker, mandatory scroll driver or animation library was added."
      },
      "primaryReferencesChecked": [
        "https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/view-transitions/same-document",
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/web-animations-1/",
        "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transforms-2/#grouping-property-values"
      ],
      "limits": [
        "One dependency-free SPA development study does not establish general router/framework compatibility or a held-out harness benchmark.",
        "Verification uses existing Chromium headless shell 151 on this macOS host, including native View Transitions. Safari, Firefox, physical devices and touch hardware were not exercised.",
        "Real-time captures and a normal-speed recording show visible motion beats; they do not establish fps, smoothness under all loads or performance gains.",
        "No actual FLIP or continuous scroll driver is implemented here; those mechanics are separate parent checks.",
        "The native callback ownership diagnostic intentionally delays capture and uses programmatic link activation. Normal rapid data navigation is exercised with real pointer links.",
        "The checker deliberately injects one HTTP 503 response to verify failure/retry. That expected resource error is recorded separately from JavaScript errors and unhandled rejections."
      ]
    },
